{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments ["<b>He who seeks</b> — that one rise at dawn to do good, he seeks to appease his fellow whom he has wronged, or he seeks favor, that HaShem accept him." "<b>And he who seeks out</b> — to do evil to his fellow, it shall come upon him from HaShem, as in: \"His trouble shall return upon his head\" (Psalms 7:17) and so forth."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:22:13.903772566Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}